&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://pages.8thlight.com/hubfs/Juan/New%20Careers%20Banner.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot;&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: Waterloo, London, England, UK | &lt;strong&gt;Hybrid&lt;/strong&gt; (1 day per week in office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we bring life to the best ideas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2006 and headquartered in Chicago, we are a technology solutions consultancy that partners with organisations from early-stage startups to the world&#39;s largest companies. We take on hard software challenges and turn them into durable results. We build agentic products, the platforms they run on, and the engineering and design at every layer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to quality means we deliver solutions we’re truly proud of, while our curiosity sparks innovation and breakthrough thinking. 8th Lights thrive in an environment that champions continuous education, fueling our growth through mentorship and hands-on work. We foster an open, collaborative culture grounded in honesty that builds trust, and believe true success is measured by the outcomes we create for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this kind of work and our kind of people energises you, you’ve found the right place.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve shown long-term repeated success on a variety of projects, typically over the course of 10+ years. You are a trusted expert and leader, often called upon to guide ambiguous initiatives and architect scalable solutions. You bring a blend of deep consulting acumen, technical expertise, and product thinking that drives measurable and impactful outcomes. In your previous experience, you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built and shipped production-grade platforms: the reusable foundations, tools, infrastructure, and workflows that help other teams shift faster and more reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taken AI and agentic systems from prototype to production, with a strong understanding of infrastructure, authentication, and observability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivered on&amp;nbsp; high-stakes consulting engagements across multiple language paradigms, stacks, ecosystems, and client industries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built high-quality, maintainable software collaboratively, incrementally, and through an approach tailored towards the unique needs of the clients you’ve served&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led the development and delivery of production-grade software using a variety of languages and frameworks, including but not limited to: Java, C#/.NET, Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Go, Ruby, Scala, R, and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively experimented with AI development tools and translated that experimentation into faster, higher-quality delivery for your teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of understanding, assessing, and embracing new tooling and trends within the software industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or integrated AI/ML features into products and systems, including recommendation engines, NLP, computer vision, predictive analytics, RAG pipelines, and agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led modernisation and replatforming efforts to align legacy systems with short and long-term business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led and delivered solutions to architecture-level problems including scalability, security, reliability, performance, maintainability, and observability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitated alignment across technical and non-technical stakeholders to move initiatives forward through ambiguity and complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provided mentorship and team support at scale, while sharing knowledge and improving team practices&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboratively led stakeholders to balance technical considerations with product and user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively sought out and effectively given feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do At 8th Light&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a go-to technologist and strategist within 8th Light, you’ll work with a variety of clients, typically one to two in a year, while continuing to deepen your and our collective domain expertise over the course of your career with us. You’ll be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly building trust with clients, demonstrating technical expertise and understanding of their domain and objectives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving platform engineering work at the client level, connecting long-term technical vision to what ships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading platform strategy and delivery across diverse platform types, connecting long-term vision to what ships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working pragmatically to balance technology choices while delivering high-quality work within deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising clients on architecture, scalability and platform evolution, connecting technical decisions to product and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating on systems that involve the full ML lifecycle from data ingestion and preprocessing, to model deployment, integration, and performance monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving innovation by proactively surfacing new technical approaches and product solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading or initiating formal feedback conversations with teams and clients via retrospectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly articulating and documenting outcomes and driving forward action items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the health of your team and 8th Light’s culture by modeling our Values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and managing high-level technical roadmaps for large engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building your network and maintaining relationships with clients and other industry leaders within your domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coaching client engineering teams, transferring knowledge and leveling up practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing client CTOs and executive decisions. Planning and execute technical work that involves stakeholders outside of project boundaries such as across a client&#39;s technical organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account teams on planning, opportunity identification, stakeholder relationships, and pre-sales scope shaping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating retrospectives, strategy sessions, and technical deep-dives to improve team and project outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying, mitigating, and resolving blockers to team progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to 8th Light by serving as a mentor, leading or designing workshops internally or for clients, representing 8th Light in the tech community, or supporting our hiring processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrating leadership in scalable system design, modular architecture, and platform- or product-oriented development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bringing depth in testing strategies, observability, fault tolerance, and secure engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying architectural patterns to evaluate tradeoffs and drive clear, documented design rationale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly Preferred Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across many areas, and encourage anyone with the experience listed above to apply. We would particularly like to encourage applicants with experience in the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform engineering: building reusable software foundations, internal developer platforms, and infrastructure that other teams build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Engineering: including platforms like Databricks for data processing and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering production agentic systems, including RAG pipelines, vector search, and agentic frameworks such as LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, AutoGen, and n8n&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevSecOps &amp;amp; DevOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MLOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building a truly diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace is an ongoing journey, and we’re excited to keep learning and growing together. We have a proud tradition of hiring talented colleagues with real-world career experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll be Supported&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we believe our people are our greatest asset. Their growth, well-being, and success shape our future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our wellness package is designed with the Whole YOU in mind and includes:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A robust L&amp;amp;D programme featuring unlimited access to thousands of books, courses, and expert-led training on the O&#39;Reilly learning platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual financial stipend and time allotment for learning &amp;amp; development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coworking support for our global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks of new parent leave available for eligible employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See our full list of &lt;a href=&quot;http://8thlight.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that is transparent, fair, and helps us attract and retain top talent in alignment with our company’s strategic growth goals and clients’ needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We benchmark our salaries using Geographic Structures to establish competitive pay ranges within the regions where 8th Lights live. Our pay ranges for our Principal Engineer position within London is: £92,818-£116,122 GBP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reach out to &lt;a ----- ----- for more relevant information pertaining to your local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8th Light Hubs and Geographies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8th Light&#39;s culture is rooted in strong connections that extend across our teams, regions, and beyond client work. We are a distributed team across the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom, with hubs in Chicago, London, Los Angeles, New York, and Seattle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London Co-working: &lt;/strong&gt;Employees working from our London hub follow a hybrid model, which includes a minimum of one day per week in our Waterloo Office. This co-working day is designed to encourage collaboration and further strengthen our community.In most cases, our consulting engagements do not require travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hope to see you apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;sup&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;A Note on Your Privacy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;At 8th Light, one of our core values is&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Honesty that builds trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; — and that shapes how we approach hiring. We want you to have a clear picture of &lt;em&gt;who we are&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;what we&#39;re looking for&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;how we handle your information&lt;/em&gt; throughout the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Before submitting your application, please take a moment to review our &lt;a class=&quot;underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current&quot; href=&quot;https://8thlight.com/global-8th-light-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. By applying, you acknowledge that you&#39;ve read it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://pages.8thlight.com/hubfs/Juan/New%20Careers%20Banner.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot;&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: Waterloo, London, England, UK | &lt;strong&gt;Hybrid&lt;/strong&gt; (1 day per week in office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we bring life to the best ideas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2006 and headquartered in Chicago, we are a technology solutions consultancy that partners with organisations from early-stage startups to the world&#39;s largest companies. We take on hard software challenges and turn them into durable results. We build agentic products, the platforms they run on, and the engineering and design at every layer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to quality means we deliver solutions we’re truly proud of, while our curiosity sparks innovation and breakthrough thinking. 8th Lights thrive in an environment that champions continuous education, fueling our growth through mentorship and hands-on work. We foster an open, collaborative culture grounded in honesty that builds trust, and believe true success is measured by the outcomes we create for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this kind of work and our kind of people energises you, you’ve found the right place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve shown long-term repeated success on a variety of projects, typically over the course of 7+ years. You can be the go-to leader for any software development engagement. You have a broad and deep range of expertise that allows you to make an immediate impact on projects. In your previous experience, you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led high-stakes consulting engagements from discovery to production&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built high-quality, maintainable software collaboratively, incrementally, and through an approach tailored towards the unique needs of the clients you’ve served&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Written production-quality code using a variety of languages and frameworks, including but not limited to: Java, C#/.NET, Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Go, Ruby, Scala, R, and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leveraged AI-assistive development tools for tasks like scaffolding, refactoring, debugging, test generation, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating AI/ML-powered features into products or systems (e.g., recommendation engines, NLP models, computer vision, predictive analytics)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Used context-appropriate automated testing to inform software design choices and catch bugs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debugged and refactored pre-existing code to incrementally improve it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborated with teams using Git, MacOS/Linux, and CI/CD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remedied architecture-level concerns such as scalability, security, reliability, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brought together people from different functions and perspectives in forums that encourage idea sharing, collaboration, and problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Made thoughtful recommendations and set direction in the face of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentored and shared knowledge with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively sought out and effectively given feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicated empathically with stakeholders and colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboratively led stakeholders to balance technical considerations with product and user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do At 8th Light&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a lead technologist on projects, you’ll work with a variety of clients, typically one to two in a year, through a variety of technologies and frameworks over the course of your career with us. You’ll lead more complicated projects, leading teams to do so. You’ll work with colleagues who share your passion for technology solutions. You’ll invest time developing your skills and sharing what you know. You’ll be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making immediate contributions to projects, rapidly building trust with clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working pragmatically to balance technology choices while delivering high-quality work within deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading architecture and software design discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating on systems that involve the full ML lifecycle from data ingestion and preprocessing, to model deployment, integration, and performance monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generating new potential solutions to challenges (technical and non-technical) in partnership with team members and clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading or initiating formal feedback conversations with teams and clients via retrospectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly articulating and documenting outcomes and driving forward action items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the health of your team and 8th Light’s culture by modeling our Values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring your team has a healthy, prioritized, estimated backlog&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing high-level project roadmaps as the team lead for large engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining relationships with client technical leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular syncs with the client to provide status updates, and for identifying and evaluating risks and presenting potential solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying, mitigating, and resolving blockers to team progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to 8th Light by serving as a mentor, leading or designing workshops internally or for clients, representing 8th Light in the tech community, or supporting our hiring processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly Preferred Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across many areas, and encourage anyone with the experience listed above to apply. We would particularly like to encourage applicants with experience in the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform engineering: building reusable software foundations, internal developer platforms, and infrastructure that other teams build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Engineering: including platforms like Databricks for data processing and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering production agentic systems, including RAG pipelines, vector search, and agentic frameworks such as LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, AutoGen, and n8n&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevSecOps &amp;amp; DevOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MLOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building a truly diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace is an ongoing journey, and we’re excited to keep learning and growing together. We have a proud tradition of hiring talented colleagues with real-world career experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll be Supported&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we believe our people are our greatest asset. Their growth, well-being, and success shape our future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our wellness package is designed with the Whole YOU in mind and includes:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A robust L&amp;amp;D programme featuring unlimited access to thousands of books, courses, and expert-led training on the O&#39;Reilly learning platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual financial stipend and time allotment for learning &amp;amp; development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coworking support for our global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks of new parent leave available for eligible employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See our full list of&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://8thlight.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At 8th Light, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that is transparent, fair, and helps us attract and retain top talent in alignment with our company’s strategic growth goals and clients’ needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We benchmark our salaries using Geographic Structures to establish competitive pay ranges within the regions where 8th Lights live. Our pay ranges for our Lead Engineer position within London is: £76,023-95,029 GBP.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reach out to ----- for more relevant information pertaining to your local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8th Light Hubs and Geographies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8th Light&#39;s culture is rooted in strong connections that extend across our teams, regions, and beyond client work. We are a distributed team across the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom, with hubs in Chicago, London, Los Angeles, New York, and Seattle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London Co-working: &lt;/strong&gt;Employees working from our London hub follow a hybrid model, which includes a minimum of one day per week in our Waterloo Office. This co-working day is designed to encourage collaboration and further strengthen our community.In most cases, our consulting engagements do not require travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hope to see you apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;A Note on Your Privacy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;At 8th Light, one of our core values is&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Honesty that builds trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; — and that shapes how we approach hiring. We want you to have a clear picture of &lt;em&gt;who we are&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;what we&#39;re looking for&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;how we handle your information&lt;/em&gt; throughout the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Before submitting your application, please take a moment to review our &lt;a class=&quot;underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current&quot; href=&quot;https://8thlight.com/global-8th-light-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. By applying, you acknowledge that you&#39;ve read it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Telnyx&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Telnyx is an industry leader that&#39;s not just imagining the future of global connectivity—we&#39;re building it. From architecting and amplifying the reach of a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://telnyx.com/our-network&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;private, global, multi-cloud IP network&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;, to bringing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://telnyx.com/resources/about-edge-connectivity&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;hyperlocal edge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; technology right to your fingertips through intuitive APIs, we&#39;re shaping a new era of seamless interconnection between people, devices, and applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re driven by a desire to transform and modernize what&#39;s antiquated, automate the manual, and solve real-world problems through innovative connectivity solutions. As a testament to our success, we&#39;re proud to stand as a financially stable and profitable company. Our robust profitability allows us not only to invest in pioneering technologies but also to foster an environment of continuous learning and growth for our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our collective vision is a world where borderless connectivity fuels limitless innovation. By joining us, you can be part of laying the foundations for this interconnected future. We&#39;re currently seeking passionate individuals who are excited about the opportunity to contribute to an industry-shaping company while growing their own skills and careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a highly technical Product Manager to own how developers discover, build on and grow with Telnyx.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Telnyx operates a global infrastructure platform spanning communications, AI inference, GPUs, edge compute, databases and real-time applications. We&#39;ve invested heavily in building the underlying infrastructure. Now we want to make it dramatically easier for developers to understand what&#39;s possible, build useful applications and get into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on product role leading a small team of six engineers across Developer Relations and Product-Led Growth. We aren&#39;t looking for a traditional DevRel leader or someone whose primary skill is managing people. We want a strong engineer with excellent product judgment who understands developer experience, builds things personally and knows how to turn developer adoption into revenue.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead a team of six: three DevRel engineers (sample apps, open source, technical content and demos) and three PLG engineers (activation, AI agents and automation, self-service conversion and expansion). You&#39;ll report to the Chief Operating Officer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build applications developers actually want to use — Lead the DevRel team in building production-quality sample applications, integrations, templates and reference implementations on Telnyx. Publish them on GitHub, maintain them and make them easy for developers to deploy and extend. Turn those applications into compelling technical content, live demos and developer distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product-led growth — Own the PLG operation responsible for moving developers from signup to meaningful usage and revenue. Use product telemetry, behavioral signals, AI agents and human intervention to identify friction, accelerate onboarding, improve conversion and expand self-service usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the developer experience better — Get hands-on with our APIs, SDKs, documentation and infrastructure. Work directly with product engineering to identify and resolve the issues that make products difficult to use. Our reference applications should continuously test whether our products are genuinely ready for developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-native growth systems — Work with Growth Engineering and RevOps to develop automated workflows for developer acquisition, onboarding, account intelligence, technical assistance and expansion. We believe small teams of excellent technical people supervising powerful automation can outperform much larger traditional GTM organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the entire developer journey — Applications attract developers. Developers experiment with the platform. PLG helps them succeed. Production usage generates revenue. The feedback from that process improves our products and informs what we build next. You&#39;ll be accountable for making that system work. .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong software engineering background. You should be comfortable building and debugging real applications, working with APIs, reading code and understanding complex infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Technical Product Manager, founding engineer, technical founder or similar role with substantial personal responsibility for shipping software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional product judgment, particularly around developer tools, APIs, documentation, onboarding and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI infrastructure, LLMs, inference, cloud platforms, real-time systems or developer infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of product-led growth, including developer acquisition, activation, conversion, retention and monetization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with AI coding agents, automation frameworks, product analytics and modern developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical communication skills. You can explain complicated technologies clearly and recognize what makes a useful demonstration or reference application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading a small technical team while remaining deeply involved in the actual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience at a developer infrastructure company is valuable. Experience personally building and growing something developers love is more important.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;ll measure success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your primary objective is growing developer-led revenue on Telnyx.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ll look at activated developers, production applications deployed, self-service conversion, usage expansion and retention. We&#39;ll also measure the adoption of our reference applications, how effectively our developer content attracts users and how quickly developers can get from signup to a working application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about applications developers actually use, not demos shipped for the sake of demos. We care about developers reaching production, not just generating signups. And we care about revenue, not vanity metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who will thrive here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Someone who would rather build a working prototype than spend a week debating a roadmap. Someone who notices a broken onboarding experience and immediately starts fixing it. Someone who understands both what makes infrastructure technically excellent and what makes developers want to use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be capable of leading six very technical people because you have the engineering ability, product instincts and judgment to make everyone around you more effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a builder&#39;s job, not a professional management job.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who can make Telnyx a platform developers genuinely love building on, and turn that into a meaningful business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-RH1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director of Product, Features &lt;/strong&gt;to lead the features teams for &lt;strong&gt;Star Trek Fleet Command, &lt;/strong&gt;based in London on a hybrid basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Star Trek Fleet Command&#39;s ongoing success goes from strength to strength. Our in-house developed 4X MMO was launched in 2018 and continues to evolve, being consistently one of the top 10 gross revenue Massive Multiplayer Strategy games on the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing, and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will own the long-view strategic planning across the game’s Features ensuring alignment between strategic vision and tactical execution. Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the business performance of the Features function, accountable for delivering game KPIs and guiding decisions which drive sustainable long term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own every aspect of a roadmap that achieves KPI goals set by you and the Product Team. Guiding cross-functional partners such as game designers, UX designers and artists to deliver a product that meets the product’s vision and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate product strategy and create engaging game mechanics and core game loops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See feature development through from concept to launch, including post launch analysis and optimization, to deliver best in class features that achieve set KPI goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engagement and monetisation for major feature releases, coordinating across disciplines to ensure smooth, high-impact launches which hit KPI targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the health of the product ecosystem, using insights to proactively identify opportunities and risks, and implement impactful features and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and create process improvements to support feature development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a high-performing team, mentoring product managers and operational staff, scaling team capabilities, and fostering a culture of ownership and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish institutional knowledge through clear documentation of experiments, retrospectives, and playbooks to ensure consistent learning and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quantitative analyses of data to provide key insights into product performance and uncover opportunities for further engagement and monetization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage player feedback and game data to inform roadmap and feature design solutions. Use competitive market research to identify future opportunities and feature best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of talented Product Managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous work experience with free-to-play games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative and qualitative analytical ability with attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of game design concepts and principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hitting revenue/metric targets on a live game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for figuring out how game economies work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An MBA or a Degree in Economics, Business, Statistics, Data Analytics, or Finance is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact ----- Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Wrike is the most powerful work management platform. Built for teams and organizations looking to collaborate, create, and exceed every day, Wrike brings everyone and all work into a single place to remove complexity, increase productivity, and free people up to focus on their most purposeful work.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Wrike is our people, not a place. As a distributed team, we own our growth, stay globally connected, and rely on the product we build to deliver impactful work alongside brilliant minds. You&#39;ll have real ownership over meaningful work, a global team that has your back, and the flexibility to do your best work your way. If that sounds like you, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our vision:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;A world where everyone is free to focus on their most purposeful work, together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll help build the very AI-powered platform you use every day, with real autonomy over the features you ship. Wrike is opening a new talent track for builders- senior engineers who take a feature from a rough idea to a production system on their own, and who use AI as a genuine multiplier rather than a buzzword. This isn’t a backfill for an existing seat. It’s a newly created role for someone who already operates autonomously and wants to keep doing that inside a company with real scale, real users, and daily production deployments. You take a high-level idea, figure out what actually needs to be built by talking to the right people, and ship it end-to-end: backend logic, frontend touches where needed, automated and manual testing, infra, and the dozen adjacent things a real feature needs. You read the existing codebase with judgment- reusing what’s solid, rebuilding what isn’t, and refusing to leave tech debt for the next person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is not optional here. You’re expected to work AI-native: using it daily to move faster, and knowing when to push back when it suggests something that doesn’t hold up. If you’ve written your own automation, scripts, or internal tooling to remove friction from your own workflow, that’s exactly the instinct we’re hiring for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ambiguous, high-level product ideas and turn them into a concrete technical plan- by asking the right people the right questions, not waiting for a fully written spec&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designed, built, and shipped end-to-end features across the full stack- including a Java/Spring backend, REST APIs, data layer, testing, infrastructure touches, and rollout- while utilizing modern frontend technologies like TypeScript, React 19,&amp;nbsp;Microfrontends, and Module Federation, alongside legacy Dart components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate a real, living codebase- deciding what to reuse, what to rebuild, and holding the line against unnecessary tech debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think in systems: anticipate second-order effects before they become incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make technical and product tradeoff calls yourself, manage the risk, and push things over the finish line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools (Cursor, Claude/Codex, our internal AI portal and MCP) as a daily part of how you build- including writing your own automations and skills where they save real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge AI output and product asks alike when they don’t hold up- critical thinking is part of the job, not a side skill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering experience, with deep comfort in Java (21), Spring, REST APIs, and SQL, TypeScript, React 19&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning features or systems end-to-end, not just executing a fully-specified ticket&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating and improving an existing, non-trivial codebase- this isn’t a greenfield role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced, hands-on use of AI coding tools as part of your daily workflow- you’re past the learning curve already&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort making decisions under ambiguity and owning the outcome, good or bad&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backgrounds we tend to see succeed here: technical founders, early engineers at startups who built the first version, small-company CTOs/Heads of Engineering, or senior engineers with active, recent open-source or side-project work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Stack:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java (21), Spring, REST APIs, SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TypeScript, React 19, Redux, Dart&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unit/integration testing, Java web stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI tooling: Cursor, Claude/Codex, Zencoder, internal AI portal, internal MCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 weeks of paid vacation + 5 RTT Recovery Days + Seniority Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave: 16 Weeks Maternity / 4 Weeks Paternity + Reserved Daycare Spot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance - Competitive Coverage - for employees + dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid Work – Flexible hybrid working model with a monthly home office allowance of €20 (hybrid) or €50 (fully remote).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public transportation: Coverage of 75% of subscription fee / Sustainable mobility package 200€/year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CSE Specific Benefits i.e. vacation vouchers, negotiated fees etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested in joining Wrike when the right opportunity opens up? Apply to our Senior Builder today. We’ll reach out as soon as a suitable role becomes available, or simply to arrange a Meet &amp;amp; Greet call.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruitment buddy will be &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/aleksandar-chernev-479785214/&quot;&gt;Alexander Chernev&lt;/a&gt;, Senior Recruiter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-AC1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Is Wrike and Our Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We’re a team of innovators and creators who solve the complex work problems of today and tomorrow.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work mode&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Wrike is our people, not a place. With 1,000+ employees collaborating across nearly every time zone, we support talent through 10 global hubs — Australia, Costa Rica, Cyprus, Czechia, Estonia, France, India, Ireland, Japan, and the United States — offering flexible ways of working that include remote work, hybrid environments, and co-working spaces across many locations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;While flexibility looks different across teams and regions, employees located near certain hubs — particularly in Prague (CZ), Nicosia (CY), Bangalore (IN), and Rennes (FR) — are generally expected to collaborate in person around 2–3 days per week, balancing the flexibility of distributed work with opportunities for in-person collaboration and connection.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our persona&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡&amp;nbsp; Smart:&lt;/strong&gt; We love what we do, and we’re great at it because this is our domain. Our combined knowledge in this space is unmatched.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💚&amp;nbsp; Dedicated: &lt;/strong&gt;We get up every day focused on helping our customers win. We’re committed to helping our teammates win, too!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤗&amp;nbsp; Approachable:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re friendly, easy to get along with, considerate, and helpful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture and Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 Customer-Focused&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We care about our customers. &lt;/strong&gt;We understand the customer journey, experience, and value derived from Wrike. Decision-making and action-taking are done with the customer in mind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤝 Collaborative&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We work as one and win together, &lt;/strong&gt;each bringing unique strengths that contribute to diversity of thought for better outcomes. Leveraging our own work management platform, we foster an environment of creative collaboration and shared achievement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎨 Creative&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We strive to succeed through continuous innovation. &lt;/strong&gt;It’s our pursuit of novel concepts that helped us create a market category. We continue to cultivate a workplace that fosters creative thinking as a means of transcending conventional boundaries and empowers us to break new ground to deliver extraordinary work management solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💪 Committed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in ownership at all levels of the organization, &lt;/strong&gt;by owning workflows from start to finish. Each member of our team is an integral part of this commitment, establishing work as a platform for personal growth and transformation, as well as collective success and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Check out our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/wrike/life/3fd588bf-73e8-47be-9b0a-1933d404ea88/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn Life Page&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wrike.com/wrike-company-culture/&quot;&gt;Company culture page&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/wriketeam&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wrike.com/wrike-engineering/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Wrike Engineering Team&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://medium.com/wriketechclub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Medium&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.meetup.com/WrikeTechClub/?_cookie-check=wtgfN9ARYGPSGd3e&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Meetup.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/wriketechclub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Youtube&lt;/a&gt; for a feel for what life is like at Wrike.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Wrike-EI_IE420969.11,16.htm&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.glassdoor.com/pc-app/static/img/partnerCenter/badges/eng_CHECK_US_273x90.png&quot; alt=&quot;Check us out on Glassdoor.&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great AI doesn’t start with a great model. It starts with a great platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The success of an AI initiative is rarely determined by the model alone. More often, it depends on the quality of the platform underneath it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Platform Engineer in our central Data &amp;amp; AI team, you’ll build the foundations that let engineers develop, deploy and operate AI workloads safely and efficiently. You’ll work on the infrastructure, automation and platform capabilities that allow teams to innovate without compromising reliability, and you’ll bridge the gap between promising technology and production reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think Kubernetes platforms, deployment automation, observability, security and developer experience. Think AI workloads built around Large Language Models, retrieval systems, graph technologies and modern data platforms. Think creating an environment where engineers focus on solving problems rather than fighting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing self-service platform capabilities using Kubernetes, Terraform and GitOps principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing graph and vector databases, and enabling model serving workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the observability of AI systems running in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating OpenAI or Anthropic-based services into our platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing LangGraph workloads on Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling GraphRAG architectures powered by Neo4j&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing deployment patterns so AI services meet the same standards as any other production workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend less time tuning models and more time making sure AI capabilities can be trusted, operated and continuously improved. This role sits at the intersection of platform engineering, software engineering and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis we don’t believe in throwing solutions over the fence. The engineers building systems are responsible for running them too, and that ownership extends to AI just as much as every other technology we work with. Your impact won’t be measured by the number of clusters you manage, but by how much autonomy and confidence other engineers gain from the platform you’ve built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to meet you if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about building platforms that other engineers love to use, and you’re happiest when automation replaces repetitive work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong background in Platform Engineering, SRE, infrastructure or distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have extensive experience building and operating Kubernetes-based and cloud-native environments, with infrastructure automation at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built and operated production environments using tools such as Terraform, ArgoCD, GitHub Actions or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand what it takes to operationalize AI workloads in production, and technologies such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Neo4j, GraphRAG, vector databases or LangGraph are familiar territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You believe observability, reliability and security belong in every design conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy improving developer experience through automation and self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see the gap between a successful proof of concept and a production-ready system and immediately start figuring out how to close it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of the result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get satisfaction from enabling other engineers to move faster and safer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently based in the Netherlands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Please do not hesitate to contact Maggie: 0623757086&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Only applications submitted through the website will be considered.&amp;nbsp;Please note that we do not work with external recruitment agencies and we will not pay any fees for unrequested CV introductions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Description:&lt;/strong&gt; Systemiq is a system-change company committed to achieving the Sustainable Development Goals and the Paris Agreement by transforming markets and business models across five key systems: nature and food, materials and circularity, energy, urban areas, and sustainable finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a certified B Corp, we combine strategic advisory with high-impact, on-the-ground work, partnering with business, finance, policymakers and civil society to deliver system change. With offices across Africa, Asia, Europe and the Americas, we are dedicated exclusively to sustainability-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strategy Associate, Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: London preferred. Amsterdam also possible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systemiq is looking for a Strategy Associate to join our Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy team. This role is suited to someone who combines strong strategic thinking with the intellectual curiosity to tackle complex sustainability challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on some of the most important questions facing companies, governments and wider society as they shift towards more circular and sustainable models. Projects can range from shaping corporate strategy and identifying new business opportunities to assessing value chains, developing policy recommendations and designing system-level interventions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can bring the core toolkit and pace of a strong strategy consultant: structured problem-solving, analytical rigour, clear communication and sound judgement. Strategy consulting experience is one route to demonstrating this. We are equally interested in candidates from other demanding analytical environments who can show the same quality of thinking and ability to turn complexity into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join small, senior-led project teams and take meaningful responsibility from the outset. You will structure problems, conduct analysis, develop insights and work directly with clients to translate those insights into practical strategic choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure complex problems:&lt;/strong&gt; break ambiguous questions into clear workstreams, hypotheses and analytical priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate insights:&lt;/strong&gt; conduct rigorous qualitative and quantitative analysis, drawing conclusions from incomplete or complex information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape recommendations:&lt;/strong&gt; translate analysis into clear, concise and practical strategic recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop client materials:&lt;/strong&gt; produce high-quality presentations, briefings and other client-ready outputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with clients:&lt;/strong&gt; work directly with senior stakeholders across businesses, governments, foundations and non-governmental organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to project direction:&lt;/strong&gt; help shape project approaches, hypotheses and emerging strategic conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trusted relationships:&lt;/strong&gt; work effectively with clients, partners and stakeholders across multi-organisation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be part of Systemiq&#39;s Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy platform, led by Partner Ben Dixon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben works across circular economy and energy topics and has advised organisations including the Ellen MacArthur Foundation, the United Nations International Resource Panel and multinational companies across packaging, chemicals and related sectors. He also leads Systemiq&#39;s work on plastics, focused on accelerating the transition towards a more circular and resource-efficient plastics system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Strategy and analytical capability&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for candidates who already demonstrate, or can quickly operate with, the core toolkit expected in strategy consulting. You should be able to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structure complex and ambiguous problems into clear components, hypotheses and analytical questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply strong analytical judgement to qualitative and quantitative information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Synthesize complex material into concise insights and decision-relevant recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and verbally, including through high-quality presentation materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work effectively at pace, managing changing priorities and imperfect information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Move comfortably between detailed analysis and the broader strategic question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience and background&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will typically bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least two years of experience in strategy consulting, advisory or another analytically demanding environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evidence of strong performance and increasing responsibility in your previous roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience contributing to strategy, investment, commercial or other decision-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong academic achievement, typically including a Master&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We particularly welcome candidates from strategy consulting, but relevant experience could also come from corporate strategy, investing, high-growth businesses, specialist advisory firms or other project-based environments where structured thinking and analytical rigour are central to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Sector interest and understanding&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be a specialist across every part of the Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy agenda. You should, however, bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An understanding of, or demonstrated ability to learn, complex industrial and consumer value chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exposure to sectors such as plastics, petrochemicals, chemicals, consumer goods, manufacturing, mobility, energy or waste management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong interest in sustainability, circular economy and the economic and strategic questions involved in system change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Location&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London is the preferred location for this role. We would also consider Amsterdam for candidates whose experience and capabilities are an especially strong match for the position.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;description__body&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
