&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud data engineering mastery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can design across the full data engineering stack — from ingestion and streaming through to warehousing, serving, and cost optimisation — on a major cloud platform (AWS strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep experience with streaming architectures — Kinesis, Kafka/MSK, Flink, or Spark Streaming — and know when each is the right choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can model the cost implications of architecture decisions and advise clients on trade-offs between throughput, latency, durability, and spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud certification at professional or specialty level is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of Python, SQL, and Spark — and strong opinions on how they should be used in production data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with dbt, Airflow, or equivalent orchestration — including how to build pipelines that are testable, observable, and operationally sound&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data quality engineering — not just validation rules, but how to build systems that detect and surface integrity issues before they reach consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, AWS CDK) and treating data platform infrastructure as a first-class engineering concern&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve operated at Principal or equivalent level — making architectural decisions that affect multiple teams, and being accountable for their outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re comfortable in C-suite and VP-level client conversations, translating technical complexity into business risk and opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You can hold a room on a difficult technical topic and reach a decision — not just present options&lt;/li&gt;
